1. Factory state
    [MC] primary: valid: version 4.2, security counter 1
    [FC] primary: valid: version 2.7, security counter 1
    [MD] primary: valid: version 1.3, security counter 1
    running: FC 2.7 MC 4.2 MD 1.3
    MC decision: all verified, combination tested -> motors may be ENABLED (arming still needs the operator)

2. The motion controller's image is modified in flash (a bit flipped by an attacker or by wear)
    [MC] primary: valid: version 4.2, security counter 1
    [FC] primary: SHA-256 of header+payload does not match the hash record
    [FC] no bootable image: recovery mode
    [MD] primary: valid: version 1.3, security counter 1
    running: FC none MC 4.2 MD 1.3
    MC decision: a processor is in recovery mode -> motors stay DISABLED (safe state)

3. The motor driver is updated alone to 1.4 (signed, valid) but 1.4 was never tested with this set
    [MD] update candidate: valid: version 1.4, security counter 1
    [MC] primary: valid: version 4.2, security counter 1
    [FC] primary: valid: version 2.7, security counter 1
    [MD] primary: valid: version 1.4, security counter 1
    running: FC 2.7 MC 4.2 MD 1.4
    MC decision: combination not in the signed compatibility list -> motors stay DISABLED

4. One key per processor: the main computer's key cannot sign motor-driver firmware
    [MD] update candidate: key hash is not one of the device's trusted keys

5. Debug port left unlocked on the motor driver (fuse not blown at the factory)
    [MC] primary: valid: version 4.2, security counter 1
    [FC] primary: valid: version 2.7, security counter 1
    [MD] primary: valid: version 1.3, security counter 1
    running: FC 2.7 MC 4.2 MD 1.3
    MC decision: all verified, combination tested -> motors may be ENABLED (arming still needs the operator)
    after boot, a probe on the MD debug port: connects; can halt the CPU and write RAM: the code that runs is no longer the code that was verified
    end-of-line check (factory test): MD debug lock = OPEN -> unit must not ship

6. Coordinated update 4.3 / 2.8 / 1.3 (the second tested set), installed and confirmed
    [MC] update candidate: valid: version 4.3, security counter 2
    [FC] update candidate: valid: version 2.8, security counter 2
    [MC] primary: valid: version 4.3, security counter 2
    [FC] primary: valid: version 2.8, security counter 2
    [MD] primary: valid: version 1.3, security counter 1
    running: FC 2.8 MC 4.3 MD 1.3
    MC decision: all verified, combination tested -> motors may be ENABLED (arming still needs the operator)
